    <item>
      <title></title>
      <link>https://wfangtw.github.io/authors/admin/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <guid>https://wfangtw.github.io/authors/admin/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;m a Founding AI Scientist at &lt;a href=&#34;https://subconscious.dev&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;Subconscious&lt;/a&gt;. My current research focuses on training and inference for effective, efficient, and long-horizon LLM agents.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;During my PhD, I worked with &lt;a href=&#34;http://people.csail.mit.edu/jrg/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;Dr. James Glass&lt;/a&gt;&amp;rsquo; Spoken Language Systems group at CSAIL.
My research focused on augmented and agentic LLMs, with an emphasis on improving LLM agents&amp;rsquo; retrieval and tool-use capabilities. I also worked on knowledge-grounded AI, aiming to ground models in factual and structured knowledge.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I hold a Master&amp;rsquo;s degree from MIT, where I worked on automatic fact verification and speech synthesis under Dr. Glass. I received my Bachelor&amp;rsquo;s degree from National Taiwan University, working on speech and language understanding with &lt;a href=&#34;http://speech.ee.ntu.edu.tw/~tlkagk/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;Prof. Hung-Yi Lee&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&#34;http://speech.ee.ntu.edu.tw/previous_version/lslNew.htm&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;Prof. Lin-Shan Lee&lt;/a&gt;, and computer vision with &lt;a href=&#34;http://vllab.ee.ntu.edu.tw/members.html&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;Prof. Yu-Chiang Frank Wang&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;!--Wei Fang is a final year PhD candidate in the Spoken Language Systems Group at MIT CSAIL, advised by [Dr. James Glass](http://people.csail.mit.edu/jrg/).--&gt;

&lt;!--His current research explores augmented and agentic LLMs, including but not limited to improving LLM agents&#39; retrieval, planning and tool-using capabilities and efficiency. He has also worked on knowledge-grounded AI, aiming to ground models on factual and structured knowledge. He is generally interested in generative AI and machine learning.--&gt;

&lt;!--Wei holds a Master&#39;s degree from MIT, where he worked on automatic fact verification and speech synthesis under Dr. Glass. He obtained his Bachelor&#39;s degree at National Taiwan University, where he worked on speech and language understanding under [Prof. Hung-Yi Lee](http://speech.ee.ntu.edu.tw/~tlkagk/) and [Prof. Lin-Shan Lee](http://speech.ee.ntu.edu.tw/previous_version/lslNew.htm), and computer vision problems under [Prof. Yu-Chiang Frank Wang](http://vllab.ee.ntu.edu.tw/members.html).--&gt;
</description>
